Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue.** The parser reads dates month first, and our tenants write the day
first. The fix is queued.

<Callout>
Known. One issue, one fix queued.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The export separates the merged reports into two causes:

- **379 reports**: the shared parser flips day-first dates. This is tracked in [issue
  #1](https://github.com/piotrowczareknext/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
- **33 reports**: the booking-v3 `MM/DD/YYYY` hint conflicts with day-first tenants. This
  is tracked in [issue #2](https://github.com/piotrowczareknext/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- A big ticket is mostly one bug reported many times. Merge early, count once.
- Write the page while the queue is still in your head.

